{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795072119,"nonce":"zTK3O1wihM/8flUN9gRcBIgsRTo=","title":"WindowConfig field for motion promotion (instead of BLINC_MOTION_PROMOTION)","message":"Since upstream 4e366fe1 the motion promotion is off by default and can only be switched on with the environment variable BLINC_MOTION_PROMOTION. The windowed runner (WindowedApp::run_with_theme, WindowConfig) has no field for it, so a library that opens a window has to change the process environment, which is unsound next to other threads (glibc) and has to be an unsafe call at the start of main.\nWe would like a field `motion_promotion: Option\u003cbool\u003e` in WindowConfig (None keeps the variable and the default) that the runner reads instead of the variable.\nWhy it matters: with the promotion off, the block menu of a text editor is drawn under the text of the area behind it (the text shows through the menu). The offscreen renderer already has the field; only the windowed one lacks it.\nWe can prepare a small PR if this is welcome.","files":null}]}